    {
      "heading": "How it works",
      "lines": [
        {
          "ar": "اِسْمُكَ",
          "en": "your name"
        },
        {
          "ar": "اِسْمِي",
          "en": "my name"
        },
        {
          "ar": "حَالُكَ",
          "en": "your condition"
        },
        {
          "ar": "حَالِي",
          "en": "my condition"
        }
      ],
      "note": "Add ka to the end of a noun to say your, when speaking to a man. Add ee to say my."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Word builder: the root ain, meem, laam, meaning work",
      "lines": [
        {
          "ar": "عَمِلَ",
          "en": "he worked"
        },
        {
          "ar": "عَمَلٌ",
          "en": "work"
